@startuml activity-refresh
' The job refresh, as an activity. The detail of each step is in the
' component design; this is the shape of the run and its two gates.
!include _style.puml

start
:ask every board for its listings, and name the ones\nthat fail, so the report can say which;
:drop the listings that have no id, no title or no\ncompany, the duplicates, and the machine-generated ones;
if (is the corpus at its cap?) then (yes)
:evict the listings not seen for the longest,\nand delete their vectors;
else (no)
endif
:admit the listings within the per-source, the\nper-refresh and the corpus limits;
:store the listings, upserted by the canonical id;
:find the texts the embedding cache does not already hold;
if (is the daily work budget spent?) then (yes)
:stop with a partial result, and set quota_exhausted;\nthe next run resumes from the cache;
else (no)
:share the remaining budget between the sources,\nthen embed the misses and nothing else;
endif
:return the report: the counts, the source errors, the\nplanned and used embeddings, and the two flags;
stop

@enduml
